rem Freshman's Product
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=778

use numbers
use sequences
use linalg
use io
use cli

arg Runs integer = 234567
arg Bound integer = 765432
arg Mod integer = 1000000009

rem Digit i of the product only depends
rem on digit i of each factor, so the
rem sum is split by digit. For one digit
rem position, the running product mod 10
rem is a state vector; one factor moves
rem state r to r d mod 10 with weight
rem cnt_i(d), the number of x in 0..M
rem having digit d at position i. The
rem matrix power gives the end states.
Size = Bound text len
Spots = 0 to Size - 1
Unit = 10 ** Spots
Wide = Unit * 10
Rows = (Bound + 1) // Wide
Rest = (Bound + 1) mod Wide
Digit = (0 to 9) reshape 1 10
Top = Unit reshape Size 1
Left = Rest reshape Size 1
Edge = Left - Digit * Top
Part = (Edge min Top) max 0
Base = (Rows * Unit) reshape Size 1
Cnt = (Base + Part) mod Mod
Line = 0 to 9
Dgrid = Line reshape 1 10 1
Rgrid = Line reshape 1 1 10
Mapped = (Dgrid * Rgrid) mod 10
Place = (Spots reshape Size 1 1) * 100
Slots = Place + Mapped * 10 + Rgrid
Cube = Cnt reshape Size 10 1
Vals = Cube + Slots * 0
Cells = array shape (Size * 100) fill 0
Cells Slots += Vals .accumulate
Mats = Cells reshape Size 10 10
Jump = Mats matpow Runs rank 2 0 mod Mod
Power = Jump
Ends = Power # # 1
Weights = (0 to 9) reshape 1 10
Sums = (Ends * Weights) sum axis 1
Plain = Unit mod Mod
Mixed = Sums * Plain mod Mod
Answer = Mixed sum mod Mod
Answer print
